{"kind":"report","text":"CHANGES REQUESTED on exact clean pushed head 78211e6ef0499852ac0a676ce53cab4301741024 and all six artifacts. Architecture: this changes the Workroom application fold and projection contract, plus its UI, embedded service, architecture page, AGENTS.md, and SKILL.md. The profile advance to workroom-fold@8 is warranted because historical decisions change, and the documented direct-report shape is coherent, but the implementation does not yet preserve that contract after a claim is withdrawn. Test reproduction: after an effective promise is retired, a later direct report on the request is effective, yet projectCommitments branches on the raw nonempty promise-dependent slice and emits only status reneged with no report. The accepted direct completion therefore disappears from the board. Add coverage that finds a reported direct commitment after the retired claim and make projection consider live claims or otherwise represent both historical attempt and current direct completion without losing either. Security: the promised arm accepts a report resting on a promise plus any unrelated request because len(promises)==1 short-circuits without verifying the request relation. An isolated test with promise on request A and report bases promise plus request B is effective. This permits false request provenance and avoidable staleness injection. Require any request basis beside a promise to be that promise unique originating request, and add a refusal test. Simplification: normalize the chosen commitment shape once and have admission, originatingRequest, latestCompletion, and projection consume it; branching on raw dependent counts is what created the retired-claim split. Baseline exact-head checks pass: focused Go packages, go vet, 83 UI tests, TypeScript, clean/pushed head and diff check. Two added isolated regression tests fail exactly on the blockers above. Any repair changes the head and requires fresh artifacts and review.","body":{"artifact":"git:sh